From: vmlab-win3d <ai@wiltaylor.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkaninfo: Load user32 on every Windows compiler

main() set up the Windows-only state under #if defined(_MSC_VER), so a
MinGW or clang (GNU driver) build skipped all of it. The skipped code
includes the User32Handles load, so user32_handles stays null.
AppCreateWin32Window then calls user32_handles->pfnLoadIconA and
crashes with an access violation as soon as an instance with
VK_KHR_win32_surface has a device to query.

Guard the Windows setup with _WIN32. Keep only the MSVC CRT debug calls
(_set_abort_behavior, _CrtSetReportMode, _CrtSetReportFile) under
_MSC_VER. SetErrorMode and ConsoleEnlarge are Win32 API calls, so
they now run in every Windows build, as they already did with MSVC.
The only other _MSC_VER use in vulkaninfo is a warning pragma
(vulkaninfo.h), which does not change behaviour.

Upstreamable: the bug is present on Vulkan-Tools main as of
2026-10-17 (vulkaninfo.cpp, main()), and the change affects only
non-MSVC Windows builds. Against vulkan-sdk-1.4.363.0.
---
diff --git a/vulkaninfo/vulkaninfo.cpp b/vulkaninfo/vulkaninfo.cpp
--- a/vulkaninfo/vulkaninfo.cpp
+++ b/vulkaninfo/vulkaninfo.cpp
@@ -1485,11 +1485,13 @@
     if (!parsing_return) return 1;
     ParsedResults parse_data = parsing_return.value();
 
+#if defined(_WIN32)
 #if defined(_MSC_VER)
     _set_abort_behavior(0, _WRITE_ABORT_MSG | _CALL_REPORTFAULT);
-    SetErrorMode(SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS | SEM_NOGPFAULTERRORBOX);
     _CrtSetReportMode(_CRT_ASSERT, _CRTDBG_MODE_FILE);
     _CrtSetReportFile(_CRT_ASSERT, _CRTDBG_FILE_STDERR);
+#endif
+    SetErrorMode(SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS | SEM_NOGPFAULTERRORBOX);
 
     if (ConsoleIsExclusive()) ConsoleEnlarge();
     User32Handles local_user32_handles;
